The track locations are shown in the second picture.

55
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:17,470
The main drawback of magnetic stripe technology is that the stored data can be altered very easily.

56
00:05:17,830 --> 00:05:27,040
Manipulating embossed characters requires at least a certain amount of manual dexterity, and such manipulations

57
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:31,090
can readily can readily be detected by a trained eye.

58
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:38,410
By contrast, the data recorded on the magnetic stripe can easily be altered using a standard read or

59
00:05:38,410 --> 00:05:43,690
write device, and is difficult to prove such changes afterward.

60
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:53,720
So what about the smart cards?

61
00:05:53,900 --> 00:06:00,200
So smart cards are the latest innovation in the family of identification cards in id1 format.

62
00:06:00,590 --> 00:06:07,370
Their characteristic feature is an integrated circuit embedded in the card body, which has components

63
00:06:07,370 --> 00:06:11,180
for transmitting, storing, and processing data.

64
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:17,900
The data can be transmitted by contacts on the surface of the card, or by an electromagnetic field,

65
00:06:17,900 --> 00:06:19,430
without using contacts.

66
00:06:19,970 --> 00:06:25,730
Smart cards offer several advantages compared with magnetic stripe cards.

67
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:34,040
For example, the maximum storage capacity capacity of a smart card is many times greater than, uh,

68
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:36,830
than the one of a magnetic stripe card.

69
00:06:37,790 --> 00:06:45,140
Chips with memory capacities in the megabyte range are now available, and the maximum capacity increases

70
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:47,150
with each new chip generations.

71
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:54,530
However, one of the most important advantages of smart cards is that their stored data can be protected

72
00:06:54,530 --> 00:06:57,320
against unauthorized access and manipulation.

73
00:06:57,920 --> 00:07:05,120
The data can only be accessed via a serial interface that is controlled by the operating system or security

74
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:12,590
logic, which means that confidential data can be stored in the card in a manner that prevents it from

75
00:07:12,590 --> 00:07:15,170
ever being read from outside the card.

76
00:07:18,330 --> 00:07:21,120
So what about contactless memory cards?

77
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:27,360
So contactless memory cards have have come into widespread use in recent years.

78
00:07:27,660 --> 00:07:35,400
Standard cards compliant with ISO 14,443 have an operating range of up to ten centimetres.

79
00:07:35,970 --> 00:07:41,490
The usable memory capacity ranges from several hundred bytes to a few kilobytes.

80
00:07:42,870 --> 00:07:50,070
The memory can be partitioned into several sectors that are independently protected against unauthorized

81
00:07:50,070 --> 00:07:52,530
reading, writing, and erasing.

82
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:58,020
This enables a single card to support several different applications.

83
00:07:58,590 --> 00:08:05,730
Each card in fact has a unique serial number stored in Rome, as well as authentication logic using

84
