So what's the difference between contact and contactless smart cards?

97
00:09:16,590 --> 00:09:23,790
So as we said, contact smart card are identified by a gold or silver chip that is visible on the card

98
00:09:23,790 --> 00:09:26,430
body, much like a computer.

99
00:09:26,460 --> 00:09:33,270
This chip contains its own operating system profile and card file structure that varies from application

100
00:09:33,270 --> 00:09:34,140
to application.

101
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:40,050
These cards are named contact due to the fact that they physically need to be.

102
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:47,580
They physically need to be inserted into a card reader to make contact with the mechanism for the most

103
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:49,950
secure mode or encrypted communication.

104
00:09:52,550 --> 00:09:59,420
In fact, the contact smart card is basically a plastic card which can be read only when it's brought

105
00:09:59,420 --> 00:10:01,430
into contact with the card reader.

106
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:04,700
It derives its power from the card reader.

107
00:10:04,820 --> 00:10:12,200
It typically has a contact area of approximately one centimeter square with several gold plated contact

108
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:12,770
pads.

109
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:17,540
The contact pads provide electrical connectivity to the reader.

110
