Communication protocols for contact smart cards are defined in ISO 7816 three specification.

111
00:10:25,340 --> 00:10:33,050
By the way, when we talk about contact smart cards, we refer always to the ISO 7816 standard.

112
00:10:33,110 --> 00:10:40,850
However, when we talk about contactless smart cards, we refer to the ISO 14,443 standard.

113
00:10:41,390 --> 00:10:49,670
And for your information, as you may know, one card can be contact and contactless at the same time.

114
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:56,720
For example, our banking card today we can pay with contact or contactless mode for the contactless,

115
00:10:56,720 --> 00:11:00,290
there is always a limit of payment of amount.

116
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:07,280
So regarding contactless smart card, in fact, contactless smart cards differ from contact because

117
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:09,050
the chip is not visible on the card.

118
00:11:09,380 --> 00:11:14,990
Instead, the chip and chip's antenna are embedded within the card body.

119
00:11:15,470 --> 00:11:22,010
The card is waved over an RFID reader instead of inserted like a contact card.

120
00:11:22,490 --> 00:11:29,690
When the contactless card passes through the specifically tuned RFID field, the antenna powers up the

121
00:11:29,690 --> 00:11:33,440
chip and relays the chip's information to the application.

122
00:11:34,250 --> 00:11:41,090
As the name suggests, contactless smart cards can be read without bringing the card in contact with

123
00:11:41,090 --> 00:11:41,540
the reader.

124
00:11:41,990 --> 00:11:47,870
The card communicates with the reader through RFID induction technology, which also powers the card.

125
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:55,550
The RFID technology used in this case works over a short range less than four inches.

126
00:11:56,060 --> 00:11:59,630
As such, the card should be held near to the reader.

127
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:07,130
The card includes an embedded secure microcontroller or equivalent intelligence, internal memory,

128
00:12:07,130 --> 00:12:10,430
and a small antenna for communicating with the reader.

129
00:12:11,090 --> 00:12:16,970
Finally, when the card is brought into the electromagnetic field of the reader, the chip in the card

130
